+# Deployment / health-check template (placeholders)
+
+Use this when reusing the flow in another repo or when you want to plug in your own URLs and doc names.
+
+---
+
+## 1. Patch with doc name placeholders
+
+Where the docs reference each other, you can use placeholders instead of real filenames so another project can substitute its own paths:
+
+| Placeholder | Replace with (this repo) | Use for |
+|-------------|--------------------------|---------|
+| `{{SHOPIFY_SETUP_CHECKLIST}}` | `SHOPIFY_SETUP_CHECKLIST.md` | Link to Shopify setup and pre-launch checklist |
+| `{{CONNECTION_STATUS}}` | `CONNECTION_STATUS.md` | Link to integration status |
+
+**Patch with placeholders (leave unchanged):** Keep `{{SHOPIFY_SETUP_CHECKLIST}}` and `{{CONNECTION_STATUS}}` as-is in the snippet below when you copy the patch to another repo; replace them only when you know that repo's doc paths.
+
+**Example snippet (placeholders):**
+
+```markdown
+After steps 1-4 pass, continue with:
+- **Shopify pre-launch** (optional): See {{SHOPIFY_SETUP_CHECKLIST}} § Before you go live.
+- **Step 1: Create PR** → merge to `main`.
+- **Step 2: DNS** → CNAME www → your-app.lovable.app (optional).
+- **Step 3: Verify deployment** → test URLs; see {{CONNECTION_STATUS}} for integration status.
+```
+
+Replace `{{SHOPIFY_SETUP_CHECKLIST}}` and `{{CONNECTION_STATUS}}` with your actual doc paths (e.g. `SHOPIFY_SETUP_CHECKLIST.md` and `CONNECTION_STATUS.md`) or leave as-is and do a find-replace when copying to another repo.
+
+---
+
+## 2. Useful curl examples (Edge Functions)
+
+**Filled in for this project:** All examples use the actual project ref and function path. Only the auth key is placeholder or env var.
+
+### Bulk product upload (Edge Function)
+
+**POST with placeholder (replace `{{AUTH_HEADER}}` with your admin user JWT; do not commit this token):**
+
+```bash
+curl -X POST "https://rgehleqcubtmcwyipyvi.supabase.co/functions/v1/bulk-product-upload" \
+  -H "Authorization: Bearer {{AUTH_HEADER}}" \
+  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
+  -d '{"action":"create-shopify-product","product":{"title":"Test","price":"0.00","sku":"test","body":"","vendor":"","product_type":"","tags":""}}'
+```
+
+**Using an environment variable:**
+
+```bash
+export ADMIN_TOKEN="your-admin-jwt-here"
+curl -X POST "https://rgehleqcubtmcwyipyvi.supabase.co/functions/v1/bulk-product-upload" \
+  -H "Authorization: Bearer $ADMIN_TOKEN" \
+  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
+  -d '{"action":"create-shopify-product","product":{"title":"Test","price":"0.00","sku":"test","body":"","vendor":"","product_type":"","tags":""}}'
+```
+
+### GET health check (no auth)
+
+```bash
+curl -s "{{FUNCTION_URL}}"
+```
+
+**With this project's URL filled in:**
+
+```bash
+curl -s "https://rgehleqcubtmcwyipyvi.supabase.co/functions/v1/bulk-product-upload"
+```
+
+- **200** = secrets OK
+- **503** = set `SHOPIFY_STORE_DOMAIN` and `SHOPIFY_ACCESS_TOKEN` in Supabase → Edge Functions → Secrets (see {{SHOPIFY_SETUP_CHECKLIST}}).
